  <doc-data|<doc-title| The <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>> measure via
  Girsanov's theorem>|<doc-author|<author-data|<author-name|N.<nbsp>Barashkov
  and M.Gubinelli>|<\author-affiliation>
    Hausdorff Center of Mathematics &

    Institute of Applied Mathematics

    University of Bonn, Germany
  </author-affiliation>>>>

  <abstract-data|<abstract|We construct the <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>>
  measure on a periodic three dimensional box as an absolutely continuous
  perturbation of a random shift of the Gaussian free field. The shifted
  measure is constructed via Girsanov's theorem and the relevant filtration
  is the one generated by a scale parameter. As a byproduct we give a
  self-contained proof that the <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>> measure is
  singular wrt. the Gaussian free field.>|<abstract-msc|60H30|81T08>|<abstract-keywords|Constructive
  Euclidean quantum field theory, Boué\UDupuis formula, paracontrolled
  calculus.>>

  <section|Introduction>

  The <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>> measure on the three dimensional torus
  \ <math|\<Lambda\>=\<bbb-T\><rsup|3>=<around*|(|\<bbb-R\>/2\<pi\>\<bbb-Z\>|)><rsup|3>>
  is the probability measure <math|\<nu\>> on distributions
  <math|<value|CS><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>> corresponding to the
  formal functional integral

  <\equation>
    \<nu\><around*|(|\<mathd\>\<varphi\>|)>=<lprime|``><around*|{|<frac|1|Z>exp<around*|[|-\<lambda\><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><around*|(|\<varphi\><rsup|4>-\<infty\>\<varphi\><rsup|2>|)>\<mathd\>x|]>\<mu\><around*|(|\<mathd\>\<varphi\>|)>|}><rprime|''><label|eq:phi43>
  </equation>

  where <math|\<mu\>> is the law of the Gaussian free field with covariance
  <math|<around*|(|1-\<Delta\>|)><rsup|-1>> on <math|\<Lambda\>>, <math|Z> a
  normalization constant and <math|\<lambda\>> a coupling constant. The
  <math|\<infty\>> appearing in this expression reminds us that many things
  are wrong with this recipe. The key difficulty can be traced to the fact
  that the measure we are looking for it is not absolutely continuous wrt.
  the reference measure <math|\<mu\>>. This fact seems part of the folklore
  even if we could not find a rigorous proof for it in the available
  literature apart from a work of Albeverio and
  Liang<nbsp><cite|albeverio_remark_2008> which however refers to the
  Euclidean fields at time zero. The singularity of the
  <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>> measure is indeed a major technical
  difficulty in a rigorous study. Obtaining a complete construction of this
  formal object (both in finite and infinite volume) has been one of the main
  achievements of the constructive quantum field theory
  program<nbsp><cite|glimm_positivity_1973|feldman_lambda_1974|park_lambda_1975|feldman_wightman_1976|magnen_infinite_1976|benfatto_ultraviolet_1980|brydges_new_1983>.\ 

  \;

  In recent years the rigorous study of the <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>>
  model has been pursued from the point of view of
  <with|font-shape|italic|stochastic quantization>. In the original
  formulation of Parisi\UWu<nbsp><cite|parisi_perturbation_1981>, stochastic
  quantization is a way to introduce additional degrees of freedom (in
  particular a dependence on a fictious time) in order to obtain an
  <with|font-shape|italic|equation> whose solutions describe a measure of
  interest, in this case the <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>> measure on
  <math|\<Lambda\>> as in<nbsp><eqref|eq:phi43> or its counterpart in the
  full space. Rigorous analysis of stochastic quantization for simpler models
  like <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|2>> (the two-dimensional analog of
  eq.<nbsp><eqref|eq:phi43>) \ started with the
  work<nbsp><cite|jona_lasinio_stochastic_1985>. It has been only with the
  fundamental work of Hairer on regularity
  structures<nbsp><cite|hairer_theory_2014> that the three dimensional model
  could be successfully attacked, see also<nbsp><cite|catellier_paracontrolled_2013|kupiainen_renormalization_2016>.
  This new perspective on this and related problems led to a series of new
  results on the global space-time control of the stochastic
  dynamics<nbsp><cite|MWcomedown|gubinelli_global_2019|albeverio_invariant_2017|moinat_space_time_2018>
  and to a novel proof of the constructions of non-Gaussian Euclidean quantum
  field theories in three dimensions<nbsp><cite|gubinelli_pde_2018>.\ 

  \;

  A conceptual advantage of stochastic quantization is that it is insensitive
  to questions of absolute continuity wrt. to a reference measure. This, on
  the other hand, is the main difficulty of the Gibbisan point of view as
  expressed in eq.<nbsp><eqref|eq:phi43>. In order to explore further the
  tradeoffs of different approaches we have recently developed a variational
  method<nbsp><cite|barashkov_gubinelli_variational> for the construction and
  <with|font-shape|italic|description> of <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>> with
  which we were able to provide an explicit formula for the Laplace transform
  of <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>> in terms of a stochastic control problem.
  In this control problem the controlled process represents the
  scale-by-scale evolution of the interacting random field.\ 

  \;

  The present paper is the occasion to explore further this point of view by
  constructing a novel measure via a random shift of the Gaussian free field
  and proving that the <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>> measure can be
  constructed as an absolutely continuous perturbation thereof. Without
  entering into technical details now let us give the broad outline of this
  construction. We consider a Brownian martingale
  <math|<around*|(|W<rsub|t>|)><rsub|t\<geqslant\>0>> with values in
  <math|<value|CS><rprime|'><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>> and such that
  <math|W<rsub|t>> is a regularization of the Gaussian free field
  <math|\<mu\>> at scale <math|t>. Let us denote <math|\<bbb-P\>> its law,
  <math|\<bbb-E\>> the corresponding expectation. In particular
  <math|W<rsub|t>\<rightarrow\>W<rsub|\<infty\>>> as
  <math|t\<rightarrow\>\<infty\>> and <math|W<rsub|\<infty\>>> has law
  <math|\<mu\>>. We can identify the <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>> measure
  <math|\<nu\>> as the weak limit <math|\<nu\><rsup|T>\<rightarrow\>\<nu\>>
  as <math|T\<rightarrow\>\<infty\>> of the family of probability measures
  <math|<around*|(|\<nu\><rsup|T>|)><rsub|T\<geqslant\>0>> defined as

  <\equation*>
    \<nu\><rsup|T><around*|(|A|)>=\<bbb-P\><rsup|T><around*|(|W<rsub|T>\<in\>A|)>,
  </equation*>

  where <math|\<bbb-P\><rsup|T>> is the measure on paths
  <math|<around*|(|W<rsub|t>|)><rsub|t\<geqslant\>0>> with density

  <\equation*>
    <frac|\<mathd\>\<bbb-P\><rsup|T>|\<mathd\>\<bbb-P\>>=<frac|1|Z<rsub|T>>e<rsup|-V<rsub|T><around*|(|W<rsub|T>|)>>,
  </equation*>

  and\ 

  <\equation*>
    V<rsub|T><around*|(|\<varphi\>|)>\<assign\>\<lambda\><big|int><rsub|\<Lambda\>><around*|(|\<varphi\><around*|(|x|)><rsup|4>-a<rsub|T>\<varphi\><around*|(|x|)><rsup|2>+b<rsub|T>|)>\<mathd\>x,
  </equation*>

  is a quartic polynomial in the field <math|\<varphi\>> with
  <math|<around*|(|a<rsub|T>,b<rsub|T>|)><rsub|T>> a family of (suitably
  diverging) renormalization constants. The presence of the scale parameter
  <math|t\<in\>\<bbb-R\><rsub|+>> allows to introduce a filtration and a
  family of measures <math|\<bbb-Q\><rsup|v>> defined as the Girsanov
  transformation

  <\equation>
    <around*|\<nobracket\>|<frac|\<mathd\>\<bbb-Q\><rsup|v>|\<mathd\>\<bbb-P\>>|\|><rsub|<value|CF><rsub|T>>=exp<around*|(|L<rsub|T><rsup|v>-<frac|1|2><around*|\<langle\>|L<rsup|v>|\<rangle\>><rsub|T>|)>,<space|2em>L<rsup|v><rsub|t>=<big|int><rsub|0><rsup|t><around*|\<langle\>|v<rsub|s>,\<mathd\>W<rsub|s>|\<rangle\>><rsub|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>><label|eq:girs>
  </equation>

  where <math|<around*|(|<around*|\<langle\>|L<rsup|v>|\<rangle\>><rsub|t>|)><rsub|t\<geqslant\>0>>
  is the quadratic variation of the (scalar) local martingale
  <math|<around*|(|L<rsup|v><rsub|t>|)><rsub|t\<geqslant\>0>> and
  <math|<around*|(|v<rsub|t>|)><rsub|t\<geqslant\>0>> is an adapted process
  with values in <math|L<rsup|2><around*|(|\<Lambda\>|)>>. Let\ 

  <\equation*>
    D<rsub|T>\<assign\><frac|1|Z<rsub|T>>e<rsup|-V<rsub|T><around*|(|W<rsub|T>|)>><around*|(|<frac|\<mathd\>\<bbb-Q\><rsup|v>|\<mathd\>\<bbb-P\>>|)><rsup|-1>,
  </equation*>

  be the density of <math|\<bbb-P\><rsup|T>> wrt. <math|\<bbb-Q\><rsup|v>>.
  We will show that it is possible to choose <math|v> in such a way that the
  family <math|<around*|(|D<rsub|T>|)><rsub|T\<geqslant\>0>> is uniformly
  integrable under <math|\<bbb-Q\><rsup|v>> and that
  <math|D<rsub|T>\<rightarrow\>D<rsub|\<infty\>>> weakly in
  <math|L<rsup|1><around*|(|\<bbb-Q\><rsup|v>|)>>. With particular choice of
  <math|v> we call <math|\<bbb-Q\><rsup|v>> the
  <with|font-shape|italic|drift> measure: it is the central object of this
  paper. By Girsanov's theorem the canonical process
  <math|<around*|(|W<rsub|t>|)><rsub|t\<geqslant\>0>> satisfies the equation

  <\equation*>
    \<mathd\>W<rsub|t>=v<rsub|t>\<mathd\>t+\<mathd\><wide|W|~><rsub|t>,<space|2em>t\<geqslant\>0,
  </equation*>

  where <math|<around*|(|<wide|W|~><rsub|t>|)><rsub|t\<geqslant\>0>> is a
  Gaussian martingale under <math|\<bbb-Q\><rsup|v>> (and has law equal to
  that of <math|<around*|(|W<rsub|t>|)><rsub|t\<geqslant\>0>> under
  <math|\<bbb-P\>>, that is is a regularized Gaussian free field). We will
  show also that the drift <math|v<rsub|t>> can be written as a (polynomial)
  function of <math|><math|<around*|(|<wide|W|~><rsub|s>|)><rsub|s\<in\><around*|[|0,t|]>>>,
  that is <math|v<rsub|t>=<wide|V|~><rsub|t><around*|(|<around*|(|<wide|W|~><rsub|s>|)><rsub|s\<in\><around*|[|0,t|]>>|)>>.
  Therefore we have an explicit description of the process
  <math|<around*|(|W<rsub|t>|)><rsub|t\<geqslant\>0>> under the drift measure
  <math|\<bbb-Q\><rsup|v>> as the unique solution of the path-dependent SDE

  <\equation>
    \<mathd\>W<rsub|t>=<wide|V|~><rsub|t><around*|(|<around*|(|<wide|W|~><rsub|s>|)><rsub|s\<in\><around*|[|0,t|]>>|)>\<mathd\>t+\<mathd\><wide|W|~><rsub|t>,<space|2em>t\<geqslant\>0.<label|eq:sde-girs>
  </equation>

  Let us note that this formula expresses the \Pinteracting\Q random field
  <math|<around*|(|W<rsub|t>|)><rsub|t>> as a function of the \Pfree\Q field
  <math|<around*|(|<wide|W|~><rsub|t>|)><rsub|t>>. In this respect is a
  formula with very similar technical merits as the stochastic quantization
  approach.

  \;

  Intuitively this new measure <math|\<bbb-Q\><rsup|v>>, is half way between
  the variational description in<nbsp><cite|barashkov_gubinelli_variational>
  and the (formal) Gibbsian description of eq.<nbsp><eqref|eq:phi43>. It
  constitutes a measure which is relatively explicit, easy to construct and
  analyze and which can be used as reference measure for
  <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>>, very much like the Gaussian free field can
  be used as reference measure for <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|2>><nbsp><cite|glimm_quantum_1987>.\ 

  \;

  As an application we provide a self-contained proof of the singularity of
  the <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>> measure <math|\<nu\>> wrt. the Gaussian
  free field <math|\<mu\>>. \ As we already remarked the singularity of
  <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>> seems to belongs to the folklore and we were
  not able to trace any written proof of that. However M.<nbsp>Hairer, during
  a conference at Imperial College in 2019 showed us an unpublished proof of
  him of singularity using the stochastic quantization equation. Our proof
  and his are very similar and we do not claim any essential novelty in this
  respect. Albeit the proof is quite straightforward we wrote down all the
  details in order to provide a reference for this fact. The main point of
  the present paper remains that of describing the drift measure as a novel
  object in the context of <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>> and similar
  measures.

  \;

  Our proof of singularity, in particular also shows that the drift measure
  <math|\<bbb-Q\><rsup|v>> is singular wrt. <math|\<bbb-P\>>. The intuitive
  reason is that the drift <math|<around*|(|V<rsub|t>|)><rsub|t\<geqslant\>0>>
  in the SDE<nbsp><eqref|eq:sde-girs> is not regular enough (as
  <math|t\<rightarrow\>\<infty\>>) to be along Cameron\UMartin directions for
  the law <math|\<bbb-P\>> of the process
  <math|<around*|(|W<rsub|t>|)><rsub|t\<geqslant\>0>> and therefore the
  Girsanov transform<nbsp><eqref|eq:girs> gives a singular measure when
  extended all the way to <math|T=+\<infty\>>.

  \;

  \ 

  <no-indent><with|font-series|bold|Acknowledgments.> M.G. would like to
  thank S. Albeverio, D.<nbsp>Brydges, C. Garban and M.<nbsp>Hairer for
  interesting discussions on the topic of singularity of
  <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>>. N.B would like to thank Bjoern Bringmann
  for some helpful comments. The authors would like to thank the Isaac Newton
